/-!
# First cohomology of a globally generated module on the exceptional curve

In Situation [Stacks, Tag 0B4W] let `X` be the blowup of `Spec(A)` in the maximal ideal and let
`i : E ⟶ X` be its exceptional divisor. This file proves that for an `𝒪_E`-module `ℒ` which is
generated by its global sections,

`H¹(E, ℒ(n)) = 0` for every `n ≥ 0`,

with no further hypothesis on `ℒ` — in particular none on `A` beyond the situation itself.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.isZero_firstCohomology_curveTwist_of_generatingSections`:
  the vanishing above.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.curveTwistUnitIso`: `𝒪_E ⊗ 𝒪_E(n) ≅ 𝒪_E(n)`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HyperplaneTwistSequence.isZero_rightDerived_tensorRightModules_free`:
  `Hᵖ(X, (⨁_{i ∈ I} 𝒪_X) ⊗ ℳ) = 0` whenever `Hᵖ(X, 𝒪_X ⊗ ℳ) = 0`, for an invertible `ℳ` on a
  quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme.

## The argument

It is the last paragraph of the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0E7H] — the one
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange.isZero_rightDerivedPlus_one_of_generatingSections`
carries out — run on `E` with the presentation by global generators *twisted*. Global generation
of `ℒ` is a short exact sequence `0 ⟶ 𝒦 ⟶ ⨁_{j ∈ I} 𝒪_E ⟶ ℒ ⟶ 0`; tensoring by the invertible
module `𝒪_E(n)` is exact, so

`0 ⟶ 𝒦(n) ⟶ ⨁_{j ∈ I} 𝒪_E(n) ⟶ ℒ(n) ⟶ 0`

is short exact too, and `H¹(E, ℒ(n))` is squeezed between the first cohomology of the middle term
and the second cohomology of the left-hand one. Both vanish:

* `H¹(E, ⨁_{j ∈ I} 𝒪_E(n)) = 0`, because `H¹(E, 𝒪_E(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ 0` — clause (4) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0B63], `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing.isZero_firstCohomology_curveTwistSheaf` —
  and `H¹(E, -)` commutes with direct sums ([Stacks, Tag 01FF]). This is
  `isZero_rightDerived_tensorRightModules_free` below.
* `H²(E, 𝒦(n)) = 0`, because the exceptional curve is a Noetherian space of dimension one, so
  [Stacks, Tag 02UZ] applies to *every* module on it. No quasi-coherence is needed.

The twist is what makes the nonnegative degrees `n` all available at once: the untwisted
statement is the case `n = 0`, where the middle term is a direct sum of copies of `𝒪_E` and the
appeal to clause (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0B63] is the appeal to `H¹(E, 𝒪_E) = 0`.

## Where this is used

It discharges the curve vanishing that clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0B64] consumes — the
hypothesis `hcurve` of `AlgebraicGeometry.BlowUpDualizing`
`.isZero_firstCohomology_dualizingTwist_of_restrictionVanishing`, which is
`H¹(E, (ω_X|_E)(n)) = 0` — *for a caller who has the global generation of `ω_X|_E`*, and clause
(3) of that tag is exactly such a caller: its datum `G` of [Stacks, Tag 0B5H] is a generating
family of global sections of `ω_X|_E`.

It does **not** discharge the curve vanishing for clause (2) itself, which has no global
generation: the normalized `𝒪_X(E)` on the blowup of the quadric cone is a module for which the
curve vanishing, and clause (2) itself, both fail.

## Implementation notes

`curveTwist A ℒ n` is `ℒ ⊗ 𝒪_E(n)`, which is definitionally
`(Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HyperplaneTwistSequence.tensorRightModules E (𝒪_E(n))).obj ℒ`; the
proof works with the functor, so that the presentation of `ℒ` can be mapped through it by
`CategoryTheory.ShortComplex.ShortExact.map_of_exact`, tensoring by an invertible module being an
equivalence ([Stacks, Tag 01CS]).

`isZero_rightDerived_tensorRightModules_free` is the companion of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TopDegreeBaseChange.isZero_rightDerived_free_of_isZero_unit`, which is
its untwisted case: that one reads the free module as a coproduct of copies of `𝒪_X` and appeals
to `preservesColimitsOfShape_discrete_rightDerived_moduleGlobalSections`, this one does the same
after composing with the tensor functor, which preserves coproducts because it is an equivalence.
It is stated separately rather than derived from the untwisted form because the image of the
coproduct cofan of `SheafOfModules.free` under a functor is a cocone over
`Discrete.functor (fun _ => 𝒪_X) ⋙ -` and not over `Discrete.functor (fun _ => 𝒪_X ⊗ ℳ)`, so it
is not a `CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofan` on the nose.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B63](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B63)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B64](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B64)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B4W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B4W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B5H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B5H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E7H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E7H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02UZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02UZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01FF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01FF)
-/

